# React Modal & Combobox Patterns

Build modal dialogs and combobox inputs using React 19 with custom hooks and CSS transitions.

## When to Use

- Creating modal overlays for forms, confirmations, or detail views
- Implementing custom select/combobox components with client-side filtering
- Managing open/close state with React context or local state
- Styling modals and dropdowns with Tailwind CSS transitions

## Quick Reference

### Basic Modal Component

```tsx
import { useState, useRef, useEffect } from 'react';
import { createPortal } from 'react-dom';

function Modal({ isOpen, onClose, title, children }) {
  if (!isOpen) return null;

  return createPortal(
    <div className="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-center justify-center bg-black/50">
      <div className="bg-white rounded-lg p-6 shadow-xl max-w-md w-full">
        <h2 className="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">{title}</h2>
